            <div xml:id="d1305-a2">

                <pb facs="1040" n="924" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg924"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of Public Works</hi></placeName>
                        [, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-03">undated</date>].</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">To the Committee representing the Mining Industry, A. J.
                    McQuatters, and other signers, Present:</p>
                <p>Referring to your petition of June 4, I beg to advise you that, as I stated to
                    you personally, although the mining law of March 19 of the current year is in
                    effect and in full force, the period of 120 days fixed for the resumption of
                    work has not yet begun to run, for the reason that the regulations of said law
                    have not been published, which this Department under my charge has under
                    consideration and which will be published in the coming month of August, unless
                    circumstances make it expedient to delay the publication referred to.</p>
                <p>This reply will be duly published in the Official Gazette.</p>
                <p>Yours very truly,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francisco Escudero.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
